# Implementation nodes' git worktrees, one per claimed node.
# Inside the repository so the human's review sees them; ignored so they are not
# committed. See .scratch/graph-workflow/map.md, the landing policy.
.worktrees/

# The git worktrees the agent harness creates for implementation workers, one per
# claimed node. Ignored so those worktrees are never committed. The entry above is
# the path the landing policy used when the manager created worktrees by hand.
# See .scratch/graph-workflow/map-implementation-rules.md, "How the worktree is made".
.claude/worktrees/
